# W2 walkthrough: your conversation with the chief of staff, and task transcripts.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains HTTP client.
# Prerequisite: a default model (m1-providers.http) and a department with a lead (m2-org.http).

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:4111
@token = paste-your-admin-token-here

### Follow the conversation live in a terminal while you go (Ctrl+C to stop): ready, then each turn
# (run-start, answer, text, tool, message, run-end).
# curl -N -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" http://127.0.0.1:4111/v1/chief/stream

### Write to the chief. "started": it answers now; "queued": once its current turn is over.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/chief/messages
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "message": "Ask research to find out what Mastra is, with one source." }

### The conversation, oldest first: your messages, its answers with the tools it used (create_task
### here), and the departments' reports, each with its task's id. Older: ?before=<nextCursor>
# @name history
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/chief/messages?limit=20
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Stop its answer (false when it wasn't answering)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/chief/stop
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The newest task, to read its transcript
# @name newest
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks?limit=1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Its transcript: the brief as the lead got it, the lead's tool calls (a delegation to a specialist,
### agent-<key>, comes with the specialist's answer), and what you or the chief sent it
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tasks/{{newest.response.body.items[0].id}}/transcript
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Follow it live, like the chief's:
# curl -N -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" http://127.0.0.1:4111/v1/tasks/<id>/stream
